I hope I'm not just repeating what others have said, but my first thought is
that any sort of GUI is going to be dog-slow on 128MB.  That wouldn't be an
issue except that the official distribution will refuse to run if it doesn't
find the X11 libraries (*forget* about Qt), whether you're using X11 or text.

You might get around this by installing the X11 libraries.  I don't think you
have enough disk for the rest of X11, but I may be wrong.  If you must install
X11, consider using Xfce or (if you can stand it)twm  for your desktop.

If you can compile your own NetHack, consider building a text-only version,
and playing from a text-only command line.



